starfive/cdns-dsi: self-heal the first-enable VSG stall (deterministic cold boot)

On a cold boot the panel came up black roughly every time: the DSI video stream
generator (VSG) is armed in cdns_dsi_bridge_enable() before dc8200's DPI stream
is stable, so it misses the initial vsync and never starts (VID_MODE_STS
VSG_RUNNING stays 0, VID_VPOS frozen). Any later DSI bridge disable/enable (the
vendor DPMS off/on) recovers it because dc8200 keeps running and the re-arm
catches a live vsync; a plain re-modeset does not.

Make the driver do that recovery itself: after arming the video path, poll
VSG_RUNNING for ~150 ms; if it has not started, disarm the video path and
force a runtime-PM suspend/resume of the DSI host (runtime_suspend stops the PPI
clock and does phy_power_off()+phy_exit(); the retry re-runs init_link() to
re-init the phy), then re-arm on the now-live DPI. This is exactly the vendor
DPMS off/on that is known to recover it. A video-only re-arm was tried first and
proved insufficient (the phy must be re-cycled). Warm modesets lock on the first
poll and never retry.

Measured on hardware (no-touch /dev/mem probe, 2026-07-16): the re-armed VSG
does NOT start within bridge_enable itself, however long it is polled (a 20 s
in-line poll came back 0 and only delayed the boot — it blocks the DRM commit
queue). It latches on the NEXT modeset from the first fb client (psplash/
fbcon/weston fb_set_par), which in any real boot follows within ~2 s; the phy
power-cycle here is what makes that following modeset succeed (without it the
panel stays black indefinitely). So: re-arm, poll only briefly, return, and let
the queued fb-client modeset complete the recovery.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor-driver integration]

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/starfive_drm_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/starfive_drm_dsi.c
@@ -1107,10 +1107,13 @@
 	int nlanes;
 	int vrefresh;
 	u32 div;
+	int i, attempt = 0;
 
 	mode = &bridge->encoder->crtc->state->adjusted_mode;
 	nlanes = output->dev->lanes;
 
+retry:
+
 	//WARN_ON_ONCE(cdns_dsi_check_conf(dsi, mode, &dsi_cfg, false));//original //7110 mode illegal,need confirm //cannot disable
 	cdns_dsi_check_conf(dsi, mode, &dsi_cfg, false);
 	//cdns_dsi_hs_init(dsi);
@@ -1234,6 +1237,51 @@
 	tmp = readl(dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_EN) | IF_EN(input->id);
 	writel(tmp, dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_EN);
 
+	/*
+	 * First-enable VSG race (known cdns-dsi defect, fixed upstream by moving
+	 * VID_EN into atomic_pre_enable + a 6.17 CRTC/bridge reorder). On this
+	 * pre-refactor vendor driver the video generator is armed here, after
+	 * dc8200's DPI is already streaming, so it misses the first vsync and
+	 * never starts (VSG_RUNNING stays 0, panel black). The vendor's own DPMS
+	 * off/on recovers it. Reproduce that: if the VSG has not started, force a
+	 * runtime-PM suspend/resume of the DSI host (runtime_suspend stops the PPI
+	 * clock + phy_power_off/exit; the goto re-runs init_link to re-init the
+	 * phy) and re-arm. The re-armed VSG does not start within this call
+	 * (measured: a 20 s in-line poll stays 0 and only stalls the commit
+	 * queue) — it latches on the next fb-client modeset (psplash/fbcon/
+	 * weston), which the phy re-cycle makes succeed. Poll briefly, return.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < (attempt ? 100 : 30); i++) {
+		if (readl(dsi->regs + VID_MODE_STS) & VSG_RUNNING)
+			break;
+		msleep(5);
+	}
+	if (!(readl(dsi->regs + VID_MODE_STS) & VSG_RUNNING) && attempt++ == 0) {
+		u32 v;
+
+		v = readl(dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_DATA_CTL);
+		v &= ~(IF_VID_SELECT_MASK | IF_VID_MODE | VID_EN);
+		writel(v, dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_DATA_CTL);
+		v = readl(dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_EN) & ~IF_EN(input->id);
+		writel(v, dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_EN);
+
+		dev_info(dsi->base.dev, "VSG stalled on first arm; power-cycling DSI host\n");
+		pm_runtime_put_sync_suspend(dsi->base.dev);
+		mdelay(20);
+		if (WARN_ON(pm_runtime_get_sync(dsi->base.dev) < 0))
+			return;
+		goto retry;
+	}
+	if (readl(dsi->regs + VID_MODE_STS) & VSG_RUNNING) {
+		if (attempt)
+			dev_info(dsi->base.dev, "VSG started after re-arm\n");
+	} else if (attempt) {
+		dev_info(dsi->base.dev,
+			 "VSG re-armed; next fb-client modeset completes recovery\n");
+	} else {
+		dev_warn(dsi->base.dev, "VSG not running after enable\n");
+	}
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_STARFIVE_MIPI_TOOL_TEST
 	tmp = readl(dsi->regs + VID_MODE_STS);
 	printk("%s,VID_MODE_STS %08x************************\n", __func__, tmp);
